{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1781877609,"nonce":"/dL9Ze8G+zm4+0HzOjXvfRwgLE4=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABGDfNIg","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/300","origin":"github"},"title":"BizzyBoat: starboard sidescan TF frame missing (earth→garmin_sidescan_starboard does not resolve)","message":"## Summary\n\nThe **starboard sidescan TF frame is missing** from the BizzyBoat TF tree: the\n`earth → bizzy/garmin_sidescan_starboard` transform does not resolve, while\n`earth → bizzy/garmin_sidescan_port` does. As a result, starboard sidescan pings\ncannot be georeferenced.\n\n## Evidence\n\nObserved while validating the new live sidescan mosaicker\n([unh_marine_autonomy#173](https://github.com/rolker/unh_marine_autonomy/issues/173))\nagainst the bag `gabby/logs/bizzyboat_sonar/2026-06-16T14-17-37+00-00`:\n\n- `/bizzy/sensors/sidescan/garmin_sidescan/sonar_image_port` →\n  georeferences fine (produces correctly-placed Massabesic tiles).\n- `/bizzy/sensors/sidescan/garmin_sidescan/sonar_image_starboard` → every ping\n  dropped with: `no usable earth→bizzy/garmin_sidescan_starboard transform`.\n\nThe starboard `RawSonarImage` messages advertise `frame_id =\nbizzy/garmin_sidescan_starboard` (the driver appends the side suffix per\n`garmin_sidescan` `FRAME_SUFFIX`), but no static transform to that frame exists\nin the TF tree. The port frame is present, so this looks like the platform URDF /\nTF publisher defines the port (and likely down) sidescan frames but not\nstarboard — or the starboard frame is named differently than the message\n`frame_id`.\n\n## Impact\n\nStarboard backscatter can't be placed on the map by anything that georeferences\noff the per-ping `frame_id`:\n- the live mosaicker (unh_marine_autonomy#173), and\n- the offline `bag_to_xtf` XTF exporter (`marine_tools/bag_analysis`).\n\ni.e. half the swath is lost for georeferenced sidescan products.\n\n## Ask\n\nVerify and add the **starboard sidescan frame** to the BizzyBoat URDF / static TF\nso that `earth → bizzy/garmin_sidescan_starboard` resolves, mounted symmetrically\nto the existing port frame (and confirm the `down` frame while at it). The\nmounting/orientation belongs in TF per the sensor-frame convention, not in the\ndriver.\n\nPlease confirm the exact intended frame name matches what the driver publishes\n(`\u003cframe_id\u003e_starboard`), or adjust whichever side is wrong.\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context)`","files":null}]}